{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit cap, interest and return deadline","requirement":"A landlord may not require a security deposit larger than one month's rent, must hold it in a separate interest-bearing account and pay 5% interest a year, and must return it with an itemized damage list within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent; 5% interest per year; return within 30 days","coverage_conditions":"All leases and tenancies of residential real property in Massachusetts.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Successor-in-interest deposit liability does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter 60, or to a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution.","penalty":"If the landlord fails to deposit the funds, to furnish the itemized damage list, or to return the deposit within 30 days, the tenant is awarded three times the deposit or balance plus 5% interest, court costs and attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2)","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts cap on amounts payable before or at start of tenancy","requirement":"Before or at the start of a tenancy, a landlord or agent may not require the tenant to pay more than first month's rent, last month's rent, a security deposit equal to one month's rent, and the key-and-lock cost.","key_value":"first month's rent + last month's rent + 1 month's rent deposit + key and lock cost","coverage_conditions":"All residential real property leases and tenancies in Massachusetts; the lessor's agent is also bound.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Regulations may authorize an optional fee in lieu of a security deposit, capped at one month's rent, which the tenant may opt out of by paying the deposit.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following:\n(i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and,\n(ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and,","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts fee-in-lieu-of-deposit offer requirement","requirement":"A landlord offering a fee in lieu of a security deposit must offer it to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy is approved, regardless of income, credit score, immigration status and similar factors, and may not set the fee using those factors.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Lessors who offer a fee in lieu of a security deposit to prospective tenants of Massachusetts residential property.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score;  and (II) not to consider such factors and categories when setting the amount of the fee;  and","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
